[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71330,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Synovial sarcoma (SS) is a malignant mesenchymal neoplasm with variable epithelial differentiation and a specific <em>SS18</em>::SSX fusion gene.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71331,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "<p>9040/3 Synovial sarcoma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>9041/3 Synovial sarcoma, monophasic</p>\r\n<p>9043/3 Synovial sarcoma, biphasic</p>\r\n<p>9040/3 Synovial sarcoma, poorly differentiated</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-12T15:24:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71332,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5A.Y &amp; XH9B22 Synovial sarcoma, other specified primary site &amp; Synovial sarcoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71333,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71334,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Synovial sarcoma, monophasic; synovial sarcoma, biphasic; synovial sarcoma, poorly differentiated</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71335,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Urogenital SS mainly affects the kidney and prostate {10935649; 22452647; 24061517; 28134577; 30789354}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71336,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal SS is associated with abdominal pain followed by haematuria {10935649; 22452647}. Intraprostatic SS is associated with dysuria, increased urinary frequency, and nocturia {28134577}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71337,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SS of the genitourinary tract is very rare. Patients have a wide age range (15&ndash;78&nbsp;years), and peak incidence is in the third and fourth decades of life {10935649; 22452647; 24061517; 30789354; 28134577}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71338,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SS harbours a unique and oncogenic <em>SS18</em>::SSX fusion gene {32141887}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71339,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The SS18::SSX oncoprotein exerts oncogenic activity by hijacking the targeting and function of the BAF complex as well as disrupting epigenetic control {29502955; 29861296}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71340,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal SS usually appears as a large, tan, rubbery mass. Cystic change, haemorrhage, and necrosis may be present. The tumour may extend into the inferior renal cava, renal hilum, and perirenal adipose tissue {10935649; 24061517; 30789354}. Intraprostatic SS has similar gross features to those of renal SS {28134577}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71341,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Monophasic SS consists of fascicles of monomorphic blue spindle cells with a high N:C&nbsp;ratio, oval to elongated nuclei, and inconspicuous nucleoli. Biphasic SS has epithelial and spindle cell components in varying proportions. Haemangiopericytoma-like vessels, wiry collagen, and dystrophic calcification are relatively common. Poorly differentiated SS with spindle or round cell morphology shows greater cellularity and nuclear atypia than other SS, along with high mitotic activity {24061517; 30789354}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Application of a novel <em>SS18</em>::SSX fusion&ndash;specific antibody {32141887} allows a sensitive and specific diagnosis of SS. In addition, TLE1 shows diffuse nuclear staining in most cases of SS, but it is also expressed in histological mimics such as malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour and solitary fibrous tumour {17255769; 19363472}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71342,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71343,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Molecular testing is strongly recommended when histology and immunohistochemistry are insufficient to establish a diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71344,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> monomorphic spindle cells showing variable epithelial differentiation, or solid sheets of closely packed small round to short-spindled cells.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> demonstration of <em>SS18</em>::SSX fusion by immunohistochemistry or molecular methods.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71345,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) or Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system may be used.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71346,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 264,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with renal or intraprostatic SS have a poor outcome, with metastases to the lung and/or other sites {24061517; 28134577; 30789354}. In general, prognostic factors include age, size, poorly differentiated histology, and stage {9888710; 10375108; 15364967; 19514087; 18997619; 20716627; 25438927}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:39:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]